# Generated at runtime. Everything a run writes goes to out/; the bare names
# below are older runs' artefacts, kept ignored so an existing checkout does
# not suddenly show eight untracked files.
.cache/
out/
output.json
output.xlsx
report.json
compare.json
views.json
views.xlsx
views_report.json

# Generated by build/build.sh
dist/
build/hecate/
build/icon.iconset/
build/_icon_1024.png

# The desktop app's SOURCE is published; what a reviewer RECEIVES is not.
#
# The line between the two is not "app vs build" — it runs through both. The
# GUI source and the build tooling describe how the thing is made, which is the
# part worth reading. The bundle, the guides written for one person, and above
# all the baked key are what gets handed over, and none of that belongs in a
# public repo.
#
# app/bundled_key.py is ignored at the top of this file, before anything here
# can un-ignore it. It holds a real API key, generated at build time.
app/__pycache__/
build/hecate/
build/icon.iconset/
build/_icon_1024.png

# A byte-identical copy of the archive.example.json already at the repo root.
# Two tracked copies of one template is how the four-dict problem started.
build/archive.example.json

# Written for the reviewer, not for this repo.
build/HANDOVER.md
build/HANDOVER_SUMMARY.md
build/HUONG_DAN.md

introduction.md
introduction.pdf
requirements.txt
.env.example

# Local working plan, not part of the shipped project
PLAN.md

# Files prepared for a reviewer. They carry real table and column names, which
# is exactly what must never reach this repo — it is public.
deliverables/
